# Test-only environment file — deliberately (almost) empty, and tracked.
#
# It carries no configuration: phpunit.xml owns every value the suite needs, and
# Laravel's env is immutable, so anything already set there wins over this file.
#
# It exists because of what happens when it does NOT. phpunit.xml sets
# APP_ENV=testing, so Laravel looks for `.env.testing` first and falls back to
# `.env` — which is gitignored, and absent both in a fresh checkout and in CI.
# That fallback read is properly suppressed inside phpdotenv
# (@file_get_contents at Store/File/Reader.php:73), but every test refreshes the
# application, and the error handler installed by the PREVIOUS bootstrap is
# still registered and does not honour the suppression. Result: one
# "Failed to open stream" warning per test, so the whole suite reports yellow
# instead of green — and a CI gate on a permanently yellow suite teaches
# everyone to ignore it (M018/S06).
#
# Do not put configuration here. Put it in phpunit.xml.
